Chapter: BoundedParamTrap

 Bounded signatures, stage B (precondition): an out-of-range argument
 traps at the callee entry. feed threads 300 into inc-byte's
 parameter, which is bounded 0..255; the entry guard traps (UD2). The
 300 reaches inc-byte through a plain-Integer parameter, so it is not
 a literal the static check could reject - the runtime guard is what
 enforces the bound.

Section: Definitions

  inc-byte : Integer between 0 and 255 -> Integer
  inc-byte (n) = n + 1

  feed : Integer -> Integer
  feed (x) = inc-byte x

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (feed 300))
  end
